  - polyglot verification
abstract: >-
  A certifiable chess laboratory built on the particle model: every
  piece is a particle that emits a threat field (the potential layer
  K3), carries a Lagrangian energy E = [M(w) - M(b)] + mu[m(w) - m(b)]
  with mu = 0.1 (the energy layer TORUS) and moves in a discrete flow
  with memory and terminations (the flow layer KLEIN). Twelve theorems
  T01-T12 cover the board algebra (D4/V4 orbit censuses 10/20), the
  move-graph edge censuses (rook 448, bishop 280, knight 168, king
  210, queen 728), mobility sums, threat-field equivariance with the
  exact pawn anomaly 176, the Lagrangian certificates, the flow
  termination t* = lcm(W/gcd(a,W), H/gcd(b,H)) with gamma = pi^4/256
  damped billiards, the closed knight tour from f5, the perft
  identities (20/400/8902/197281/4865609), splitmix64 Zobrist hashing
  (1562 keys), the alpha-beta bounds (up to x256.8 node gain), and
  the retrograde KRK/KQK tablebases (max DTM 16 and 10 moves, zero
  Bellman violations). The protocol C1-C9 is fully reproducible by
  one command; the polyglot battery C1-C10 runs in seven languages
  with a bit-identical verdict 10/10.
